{"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/ServiceReference"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/servicereference"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" — the RevenueCat-backed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer that the paywall plugin consumes."}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatPaywallService"},{"text":" adapts ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCat.Purchases"},{"text":" to the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"text":" protocol that ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall.PaywallPlugin"},{"text":" requires. It does one job: translate ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomerInfo"},{"text":" into ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntitlementSnapshot"},{"text":" (defined by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"text":") so the plugin can drive its state. Configuration of the RevenueCat SDK itself remains the caller’s responsibility.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For a step-by-step integration walkthrough, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/HowToImplementService","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". For the entitlement-mapping rules, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/EntitlementMapping","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Library-target","text":"Library target","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Product: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Import: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Package.swift"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":[".product(name: \"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\", package: \"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\"),"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Types","text":"Types","level":2},{"type":"heading","anchor":"docSwiduxRevenueCatPaywalldocumentationSwiduxRevenueCatPaywallRevenueCatPaywallService","text":"``doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallService``","level":3},{"type":"codeListing","code":["public struct RevenueCatPaywallService: PaywallService {","    public init(","        entitlementID: String,","        permanentLicenseEntitlementID: String? = nil","    )","","    public func customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","    public func customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot>","    public func restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Value type. Holds two ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"text":" identifiers and forwards every call to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Purchases.shared"},{"text":". Cheap to construct and pass into ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"text":" — after ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatPaywall.configure"},{"text":" has run. For production, wrap it in SwiduxPaywall’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ResilientPaywallService"},{"text":" so a transient read failure at launch never gates a paid user as free.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Initializer","text":"Initializer","level":4},{"type":"codeListing","code":["public init(","    entitlementID: String,","    permanentLicenseEntitlementID: String? = nil",")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entitlementID"},{"text":" — RevenueCat entitlement identifier that grants pro access. Surfaces as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntitlementSnapshot.isPro"},{"text":" when active.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"permanentLicenseEntitlementID"},{"text":" — Optional secondary identifier for a lifetime \/ permanent entitlement. Surfaces as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntitlementSnapshot.hasPermanentLicense"},{"text":" when active. Pass ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" if the app has no separate lifetime SKU.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Important","style":"important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywall\/configure(apiKey:appUserID:userDefaults:logLevel:entitlementVerification:purchasesAreCompletedBy:storeKitVersion:)"},{"type":"text","text":" before constructing the service. The initializer preconditions on the SDK being configured — failing fast with a named fix instead of letting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Purchases.shared"},{"type":"text","text":" trap opaquely at first use. Previews and tests should construct "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"customerInfo-async-throws-%3E-EntitlementSnapshot","text":"`customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot`","level":4},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"One-shot fetch. Calls ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Purchases.shared.customerInfo()"},{"text":" and maps the result.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Throws whatever the RevenueCat SDK throws (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ErrorCode.networkError"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".offlineConnectionError"},{"text":", etc.). The plugin catches the error and dispatches ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refreshFailed(message)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"customerInfoStream-%3E-AsyncStream%3CEntitlementSnapshot%3E","text":"`customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot>`","level":4},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Long-lived stream. Wraps ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Purchases.shared.customerInfoStream"},{"text":" and yields a new ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntitlementSnapshot"},{"text":" for every change RevenueCat reports — purchase, refund, family-share update, sandbox renewal.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The stream finishes when the underlying RevenueCat stream finishes. The plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".observeCustomerInfo"},{"text":" effect normally keeps it alive for the duration of the session; cancel by cancelling the consuming ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"text":", which terminates the stream and tears down the bridge.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The stream buffers only the newest snapshot: each yield is a complete entitlement state, so a slow consumer sees the latest value rather than replaying stale intermediate states.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"restorePurchases-async-throws-%3E-EntitlementSnapshot","text":"`restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot`","level":4},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps the result of a restore. Reads ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Purchases.shared.purchasesAreCompletedBy"},{"text":" live and branches: observer mode (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".myApp"},{"text":") calls ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"syncPurchases()"},{"text":", the default mode calls ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restorePurchases()"},{"text":". In observer mode the SDK’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restorePurchases()"},{"text":" can alias or transfer purchases between accounts, so the service uses ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"syncPurchases()"},{"text":" automatically — no special-casing in your app code. Throws whatever the SDK throws on error.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".restorePurchases"},{"text":" action wraps this call and dispatches ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".customerInfoUpdated"},{"text":" on success or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refreshFailed"},{"text":" on error.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Entitlement-mapping","text":"Entitlement mapping","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For every ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomerInfo"},{"text":" the service receives:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Configuration"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isPro"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasPermanentLicense"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entitlementID"},{"type":"text","text":" active"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"(next column)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entitlementID"},{"type":"text","text":" inactive or missing"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"(next column)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"permanentLicenseEntitlementID == nil"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"—"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"permanentLicenseEntitlementID"},{"type":"text","text":" active"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"—"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"permanentLicenseEntitlementID"},{"type":"text","text":" inactive or missing"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"—"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Both flags are checked independently against the same ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomerInfo"},{"text":". A user with both active subscription and lifetime entitlements gets both flags set. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/EntitlementMapping","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for the reasoning behind the truth table.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Service Reference","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"}]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/HowToImplementService"